R-PH6 R-PH7 R-PH9 R-BL3 R-BL6 R-LF3 R-H6 R-DL5 R-EC13 R-SO7 R-RP2 R-AL6 R-NI5: no compiler download in P0, and `--no-check`. 4 runs of `update json` on 4 copies of one project, with the compiler `nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029` on PATH. Run 1: the header has the roc pin `nightly-2026-10-09-258ab27`, which is not the roc on PATH. The change needs a probe, the pin names a compiler that is a required download, and P0 refuses it with exit 13 and the message of R-PH7 (no flag name). Talon makes no copy and no probe, writes nothing, and does not download. Run 2: the same header with `--no-check`: no probe runs, so no compiler is needed (R-BL3: --no-check skips the baseline and its download). The header gets the new json and keeps its pin. The output says `check: skipped` (R-BL6). Run 3: a header with no roc pin and `--no-check`: json moves and no pin is written (R-H6). Run 4: the pin is the same other compiler but json is the newest already: nothing to change, so no probe is needed and no refusal comes.
